## 2. Tech stack — fixed

| Layer | Choice | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Language | Python 3.11+ | Type hints mandatory on all public functions |
| API framework | FastAPI | Async-first |
| Server | Uvicorn (dev) / Gunicorn + UvicornWorker (prod) | |
| Database | MongoDB 6+ | Via **Motor** (async). Never PyMongo in request paths |
| Validation | Pydantic v2 | `model_config`, `Field`, `field_validator` — not v1 syntax |
| Admin panel | Jinja2 + handwritten HTML/CSS + vanilla JS | |
| Migrations | Custom scripts in `migrations/` | Idempotent, numbered |
| Tests | pytest + pytest-asyncio + mongomock-motor / test DB | |
| Lint/format | ruff + black (line length 100) | |

### Hard bans

- **No ORM/ODM** (no Beanie, MongoEngine, SQLAlchemy). Use Motor collections plus
  Pydantic models directly.
- **No frontend framework** in the admin panel. No React, Vue, Svelte, jQuery,
  Bootstrap, Tailwind CDN. Handwritten CSS only, using the tokens in
  `color_palette.md`.
- **No blocking I/O** inside `async def` route handlers. If a library is sync-only,
  wrap it in `anyio.to_thread.run_sync`.
- **No business logic in route handlers.** Handlers parse, delegate, and return.
- **No raw dicts crossing layer boundaries.** Services accept and return Pydantic
  models or typed dataclasses.

