## 9. Admin panel rules

- Server-rendered Jinja2. Progressive enhancement only: every page must work with
  JavaScript disabled for read operations and basic forms.
- **Design tokens come from `color_palette.md`.** `admin/static/css/tokens.css` is
  the single source of color truth and must match that file exactly. If you change a
  color, change `color_palette.md` in the same commit.
- Material 3 color roles. Light and dark themes, toggleable, persisted in
  `localStorage` under `ui.theme`, with `prefers-color-scheme` as the default. Set
  `data-theme="light|dark"` on `<html>` before first paint (inline script in
  `<head>`) to avoid a flash.
- **Never use the default Material purple.** No `#6750A4`, `#D0BCFF`, `#EADDFF`,
  `#21005D`, or any near-neighbor of the baseline M3 purple palette anywhere —
  CSS, SVG, charts, email templates, placeholder art.
- Responsive, mobile-first. Breakpoints: 0–599 compact, 600–904 medium,
  905–1239 expanded, 1240+ large. Navigation is a bottom bar on compact, a rail on
  medium, a drawer on expanded+. Tables collapse to stacked cards below 600px — no
  horizontal scroll bars as the primary mobile strategy.
- Touch targets ≥ 48×48 CSS px. Body text ≥ 16px. Never disable zoom.
- Accessibility is not optional: semantic landmarks, labelled form controls, visible
  `:focus-visible` outlines, 4.5:1 contrast for text in both themes,
  `prefers-reduced-motion` respected.
- Use CSS Grid/Flexbox, logical properties (`margin-inline`, `padding-block`), and
  `clamp()` for fluid type. No CSS-in-JS, no utility-class soup.
- Frame editor (`js/frames.js`): canvas overlay on the uploaded image, draggable and
  resizable placeholder boxes, numeric inputs bound two-way to the boxes, rotation
  handle, elevation stepper. Autosave is off — explicit "Save placeholders" only.

