## 11. Code style

- Async everywhere in the request path. Name async functions plainly (`get_category`,
  not `get_category_async`).
- Type hints on every function signature, including `-> None`.
- Pydantic models are the boundary contract: `XxxCreate`, `XxxUpdate` (all fields
  optional), `XxxOut`, `XxxInDB`. Don't reuse one model for all four.
- Raise domain errors (`NotFoundError`, `ConflictError`, `ValidationError`,
  `PermissionError`) from services; translate to HTTP in exception handlers. Do not
  raise `HTTPException` outside `api/`.
- Structured logging (JSON) with `request_id` on every line. Log levels: DEBUG for
  dev tracing, INFO for lifecycle, WARNING for degraded, ERROR for failures.
- Configuration comes from environment variables only. No secrets in code, fixtures,
  tests, or comments. `.env.example` lists every variable with a safe placeholder.
- Docstrings on every service method: one line of what, one line of why if
  non-obvious. Skip docstrings on trivial repository passthroughs.
- Comments explain *why*, never *what*.

