## 12. Testing

- Every new endpoint ships with: a happy-path test, an auth-failure test (missing
  key, wrong scope, wrong instance), and a validation-failure test.
- Bulk endpoints additionally need a partial-failure test asserting the 207 body.
- Reference logic needs tests proving: (a) an instance-scoped create is rejected with
  `INSTANCE_CANNOT_CREATE_CONTENT`; (b) editing an instance item writes only to
  `overrides` and leaves the central document byte-identical; (c) deleting an instance
  item leaves the central document intact and still visible to other instances;
  (d) a central edit is reflected in a non-overridden field but not in an overridden
  one; (e) a central delete makes the reference unresolvable rather than corrupting
  the instance list.
- Frame parsing needs a test with a known fixture image and expected coordinates
  within a tolerance.
- Tests run against a real MongoDB in CI (service container), not mocks, for
  repository tests. Service tests may mock repositories.
- No test may depend on another test's data. Each uses a fresh database name.

